SUMMARY:AVL UX - A First “get to know” the UX community
DESCRIPTION:AVL Digital Nomads\nAVL UX (hosted by AVL Digital Nomads) is A
 sheville’s new meetup for UX\, product\, and research folks. This first 
 event is casual and low-pressure and focuses on- quick intros\, small-grou
 p chats\, and a short “what should we do next?” moment.\n\nWhat if Ash
 eville had a regular place where UX people could actually find each other 
 and it without\, feeling like a stiff “networking event”? **AVL UX is 
 Asheville’s new meetup for UX\, product\, and research meant to build an
 d connect the local community to shape what the**\n**UX scene here becomes
 .**\n\nThis first gathering is intentionally **friendly + low-pressure**. 
 Come as you are: working designer\, researcher\, PM\, engineer\, student\,
  career-switcher\, or just UX-curious. The goal is simple: meet people\, t
 rade notes\, and leave with new connections (and a clearer idea of what AV
 L UX should be next).\n\n**What to expect**\n\n* Quick welcomes + name tag
 s (so it’s easy to meet people).\n* Casual small-group conversations and
  prompts (And hopefully no awkward interactions).\n* A short “what shoul
 d AVL UX do next?” moment (talks\, portfolio nights\, design jams\, a Co
 nfig watch party 2026\, etc.)\n\n**A few topics up for discussion**\n\n* *
 *What’s your Asheville UX Scene?:** Where is everyone and what is everyo
 ne doing in Asheville? Why UX here as the industry is rather small\n* **De
 sign-to-code + vibe-coding workflows:** what’s actually working with too
 ls like Figma Make/MCP + Cursor—and what breaks in real teams?\n* **Acce
 ssibility is becoming the baseline:** how are you baking WCAG 2.2 into des
 ign + dev early (instead of last-minute fixes)?\n* **Design systems + toke
 ns in 2026:** how do we keep tokens clean\, scalable\, and synced between 
 design + code without “token rot”?\n* **Calm\, mindful UX:** how do we
  reduce cognitive load and create more “human” experiences instead of 
 noisy\, attention-grabby UI?\n\nFor our first meeting we’ll go to Hi-Wir
 e Brewing in RAD. Easy to get to with plenty of parking. A great assortmen
 t of both alcoholic and non-alcoholic beverages. Typically there is a food
  truck as well.\n\nLooking forward to meeting everyone and launching our n
 ew UX community!
